v 3
d undummy. Recombine a set of dummy/indicator variables into one categorical variable.
d
d undummy reverses one-hot/dummy coding: it collapses a set of
d mutually exclusive indicator variables (numeric or string) back
d into a single categorical variable, with value labels taken from
d an existing label, from the dummy variable names, or stored under
d a new label name. It verifies that the dummies are mutually
d exclusive before combining and can run that check alone. Useful
d for agency extracts and survey-platform exports that deliver one
d column per category.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or later. No other dependencies.
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260706
d
